    <string-array name="gentle_messages">
        <item>One small step is enough today.</item>
        <item>Showing up matters more than being perfect.</item>
        <item>You can begin again right now.</item>
        <item>A slip is information, not a verdict.</item>
        <item>Be as kind to yourself as you would be to a friend.</item>
        <item>Rest is part of growth.</item>
        <item>Tiny actions add up quietly.</item>
        <item>You do not have to feel ready to start.</item>
        <item>Today only needs to be a little better than a bad day.</item>
        <item>Breathe slowly. You have more time than it feels.</item>
        <item>Progress is rarely a straight line.</item>
        <item>You came back. That is the whole skill.</item>
        <item>Choose the next small thing, only that.</item>
        <item>Your worth is not your productivity.</item>
        <item>Hard days still count.</item>
        <item>Notice the urge, let it pass like a wave.</item>
        <item>You are building a life, not passing a test.</item>
        <item>Two minutes is a real start.</item>
        <item>Drink some water and stretch a little.</item>
        <item>A walk can change the mood of a whole day.</item>
        <item>You have survived every hard day so far.</item>
        <item>Let good enough be good enough.</item>
        <item>Slow is still moving.</item>
        <item>Gentle discipline lasts longer than harsh discipline.</item>
        <item>Today, protect your sleep.</item>
        <item>It is okay to ask someone for help.</item>
        <item>Thank someone today, it lifts you too.</item>
        <item>Remember why you started, softly.</item>
        <item>You can do hard things in small pieces.</item>
        <item>Your phone can wait. Your attention is precious.</item>
        <item>Start before you feel motivated.</item>
        <item>Every returning counts as a win.</item>
        <item>Look at how far you have come, not only how far is left.</item>
        <item>One honest minute of rest beats an hour of guilt.</item>
        <item>What would the calm version of you do next?</item>
        <item>Peace grows from small, repeated choices.</item>
        <item>You are allowed to take it one hour at a time.</item>
        <item>Failure to be perfect is not failure to grow.</item>
        <item>A good routine is one you can keep on a bad day.</item>
        <item>You are learning, and learning is messy.</item>
        <item>Say a quiet prayer or take a deep breath, whichever you need.</item>
        <item>Today is a fresh page.</item>
        <item>Be patient: roots grow before leaves.</item>
        <item>Keep going gently.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="urge_lines">
        <item>Notice the urge. Where do you feel it in your body?</item>
        <item>Breathe in for four, out for six. You do not have to act.</item>
        <item>Urges rise, peak and fall like a wave. Keep watching.</item>
        <item>It is already weaker than a minute ago. Keep breathing.</item>
        <item>You are the one watching the urge, not the urge itself.</item>
        <item>Almost there. Let it pass.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="replace_actions">
        <item>Drink a glass of water slowly.</item>
        <item>Do 10 slow squats or push-ups.</item>
        <item>Step outside and look at the sky.</item>
        <item>Wash your face with cool water.</item>
        <item>Call or message someone kind.</item>
        <item>Make wudu and pray two rak\'ahs.</item>
        <item>Write down what you feel in three lines.</item>
    </string-array>
