    <string-array name="recovery_steps">
        <item>Pause and breathe slowly three times.</item>
        <item>Name what happened in one neutral sentence, without blaming yourself.</item>
        <item>Ask what the trigger was: time, place, feeling.</item>
        <item>Choose one small action for the next hour that moves you the other way.</item>
        <item>Return to your routine at the next prayer. Today is not ruined.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="english_w1">
        <item>Learn the alphabet sounds and greetings (hello, how are you).</item>
        <item>Say 5 sentences about yourself out loud.</item>
        <item>Learn 10 words about family and daily life.</item>
        <item>Listen to one slow English lesson for 10 minutes.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="english_w2">
        <item>Practice present simple: I work, he works.</item>
        <item>Learn 10 words about food and shopping.</item>
        <item>Write 5 sentences about your day.</item>
        <item>Order food or ask a price in a role play.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="english_w3">
        <item>Practice past simple: I went, I saw.</item>
        <item>Learn 10 words about travel and places.</item>
        <item>Tell a short story of your weekend in 6 sentences.</item>
        <item>Watch a short English video with subtitles.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="english_w4">
        <item>Practice future with will and going to.</item>
        <item>Learn 10 words about work and study.</item>
        <item>Write a short message or email in English.</item>
        <item>Have a 5-minute speaking practice and record yourself.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="exercise_titles">
        <item>Question your assumption</item>
        <item>Say it clearly</item>
        <item>Confidence step</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="exercise_texts">
        <item>Pick a belief you hold strongly. Write one reason it could be wrong and one fact that supports it. Decide what would change your mind.</item>
        <item>Pick a point you want to make. Say it in two sentences: the point, then one reason. Then listen to a reply without interrupting.</item>
        <item>Choose one small thing that makes you slightly nervous, like asking a question. Do it today and write how it went.</item>
    </string-array>
